Package: vacttmle
Title: Visit-Aligned Continuous-Time TMLE for Trials with Treatment Switching and Censoring
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("David", "McCoy", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "david_mccoy@berkeley.edu")
  )
Author: David McCoy
Maintainer: David McCoy <david_mccoy@berkeley.edu>
Description: Visit-aligned continuous-time targeted minimum loss estimation
    (VA-CT-TMLE) for scheduled-visit randomized trials in which treatment
    switching (crossover) and loss to follow-up occur in continuous time while
    covariates are recorded only at scheduled visits. The package estimates
    failure-free survival and risk differences under the ICH E9(R1)
    treatment-policy (intention-to-treat) and hypothetical no-switching
    (per-protocol) strategies from exact switch and dropout dates, with
    influence-function inference, positivity diagnostics, and percentile
    weight control. A composite-endpoint estimator is also provided. Methods
    are described in McCoy (2026).
